<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Mr. Tagore returns four weeks after the failed trial without catheter to decide on treatment. He has read the information and talked with his family. He has had no fever, pain, blood, or leakage, and the catheter was changed on schedule by the clinic nurse. He has had no dizziness, falls, or breast tenderness. He has brought his questions written out, and he speaks about his choice in his own terms: he fears being put to sleep and cut more than he fears the illness itself, and he would rather live with the tube for a while longer than risk losing his clear mind after an operation at his age. He wants the gentlest path that lets him keep writing and teaching, and he is willing to try again without the catheter once the tablets have had time to work. He asks that his herbal preparation be allowed to continue. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Interval change</td><td>No infection, falls, or side effects; catheter changed on schedule</td></tr><tr><td>His decision</td><td>Defer any operation or procedure; keep the catheter; try again without it after three to four months of finasteride</td></tr><tr><td>His reasons</td><td>Fears anesthesia and an operation more than the illness; wants to keep his mind clear and keep working</td></tr><tr><td>Herbal preparation</td><td>Wishes to continue it</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

